"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[26243],{626243:n=>{n.exports='# Notebooks Commands\n\nCommands for managing notebook cells via `runDatabricksPrivateCli`.\n\n## notebooks list-content\n\nList all cells in a notebook by its numeric ID.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nnotebooks list-content <notebookId>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument       | Required | Description                                |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `<notebookId>` | Yes      | Numeric notebook ID (positional or `--id`) |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nnotebooks list-content 12345\nnotebooks list-content --id 12345\n```\n\nReturns cell metadata including each cell\'s `nuid` (unique identifier), content, language, and position.\n\n## notebooks edit\n\nEdit a notebook: add, update, or delete cells.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id <notebookId> --operation <add|update|delete> [--target <nuid>] [--content <text>] [--position <n>] [--title <text>]\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument      | Required | Description                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--id`        | Yes      | Numeric notebook ID                            |\n| `--operation` | Yes      | Edit operation: `add`, `update`, or `delete`   |\n| `--target`    | No       | Cell nuid — required for `update` and `delete` |\n| `--content`   | No       | Cell content — required for `add` and `update` |\n| `--position`  | No       | Cell position index (used for `add`)           |\n| `--title`     | No       | Cell title (used for `add`)                    |\n\n### Add a Cell\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation add --content \'print("hello world")\' --position 0\n```\n\n### Update a Cell\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation update --target abc123 --content \'print("updated")\'\n```\n\n### Delete a Cell\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation delete --target abc123\n```\n\n### Using --json for Complex Content\n\nWhen cell content contains special characters, quotes, or multi-line code, use `--json`:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --json \'{"operation": "add", "content": "import pandas as pd\\ndf = pd.read_csv(\\"data.csv\\")\\nprint(df.head())", "position": 0}\'\n```\n\n## notebooks execute\n\nExecute a notebook cell by its nuid on the attached cluster.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nnotebooks execute <cellId>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument   | Required | Description                                                   |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<cellId>` | Yes      | Cell identifier (nuid) to execute (positional or `--cell-id`) |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nnotebooks execute abc123\nnotebooks execute --cell-id abc123\n```\n\nReturns the execution output from the cell.\n\n## Common Workflow\n\n### Inspect then Edit\n\n1. List cells to see notebook structure and find nuids:\n\n```\nnotebooks list-content 12345\n```\n\n2. Update a specific cell using its nuid:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation update --target abc123 --content \'new code here\'\n```\n\n3. Execute the updated cell to verify:\n\n```\nnotebooks execute abc123\n```\n\n### Build a Notebook from Scratch\n\n1. Add a markdown header cell:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation add --content \'# Analysis Notebook\' --position 0\n```\n\n2. Add code cells:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation add --content \'import pandas as pd\' --position 1\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation add --content \'df = spark.table("main.default.my_table")\' --position 2\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- Always use `notebooks list-content` first to discover cell nuids before editing or executing.\n- The `--json` flag is preferred for multi-line or complex cell content.\n- Cell positions are zero-indexed.\n- `update` and `delete` operations require the cell `nuid` via `--target`.\n'}}]);
